From d0b9046267d6c0fa2fb68c787a7f3b6d5aab34f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taniya Das <taniya.das@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 30 May 2024 12:57:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] DNM: clk: qcom: Add support for Clock Debug for QCOM drivers

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [internal-only debug feature, marked DNM]

Add a clock debug infrastructure for Qualcomm clock drivers that provides:

- Hardware clock rate measurement via a debug mux, sampling the clock
  against an XO/4 reference (~27ms measurement window).
- A 'debug_suspend' debugfs entry that, when enabled, hooks into the
  machine_suspend trace point and dumps all enabled clocks to the kernel
  log at suspend time, aiding suspend/resume debugging.
- A 'debug_suspend_atomic' mode that avoids mutex-grabbing in atomic
  context during the suspend path.
- A 'clk_enabled_list' debugfs file listing all currently enabled clocks
  with their rate and enable/prepare state.

Wire the .debug_init callback into all clk_ops variants across
clk-alpha-pll, clk-branch, clk-rcg2, clk-rpmh and clk-smd-rpm so every
registered clock is automatically tracked.

Change-Id: Ic9d51bd152f5002da88e3c7dac4f2b76a94abb5d
Signed-off-by: Taniya Das <taniya.das@oss.qualcomm.com>
